- surfaces/table: grip drag-to-reorder with a jade drop line. Row and column
  moves already have two homes (the menu and Alt+Arrows), so the drag is the
  gesture form of an existing verb, not a missing capability. Reuse the shared
  drop-line plugin when it exists rather than building a second one.
- surfaces/table: while the pointer is inside a nested table's hover zone the
  outer table shows no chrome at all: one hover owner, and the inner reveal
  holds it (`nestedCellKeepsReveal`, needed at every depth). Making outer-row
  verbs reachable without leaving the inner zone changes the one-owner model
  and needs a design decision before any code.
- surfaces/table: the table's own verbs (header row, placement, reset widths)
  have no keyboard twin. The table's keys are Tab, Alt+Arrows, Enter and Esc,
  with no door to its menu; a twin needs a design decision, not an invented
  binding.
